::JOUR_U01_L03_GP_Q01::[MLA.JOUR.MED.09] Scenario: A printed school bulletin becomes a website updated twice a week. What technology change is shown? {
=A. Print distribution to web distribution#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~B. Interviewing to fiction writing#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~C. Editorial writing to poetry#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~D. Private notes to private notes#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L03_GP_Q02::[MLA.JOUR.MED.09] A mobile alert can help journalism audiences because it: {
~A. removes the need for verification#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
=B. shares urgent verified information quickly#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~C. turns every story into opinion#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~D. makes sources unnecessary#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L03_GP_Q03::[MLA.JOUR.MED.09] What responsibility increases when news can be published immediately? {
~A. Ignoring corrections#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~B. Using fewer facts#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
=C. Verifying information before fast distribution#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~D. Making stories fictional#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L03_GP_Q04::[MLA.JOUR.DIG.01] A digital presentation about a school event should organize information so the audience can: {
~A. guess the source#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~B. avoid the main facts#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~C. see decoration only#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
=D. understand the verified idea clearly#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L03_GP_Q05::[MLA.JOUR.MED.08] Which statement gives the most balanced judgment about new journalism technology? {
=A. New tools can improve access, but journalists must still verify facts.#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~B. New tools make every story correct.#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~C. Older media never used facts.#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~D. Faster publishing means less responsibility.#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
